>But some monsters can sometimes do two curse attacks within one player
>turn, AFAIK..

More to the point, each curse attack applies 1-6 curses (or 1-3 if you
are magic-resistant or have a half-spell-damage artifact, or 1-2 if
you have both defences), each assigned to a random object in your
inventory; there is no check to make sure that all the curses land on
different objects (this cuts both ways; there's also no check to make
sure that all the curses land on objects that aren't already cursed).
Thus, it is possible for a single cursing attack to take your two-hander
from blessed to cursed (although unlikely if you have a decent number of
objects in your pack).

So, you should check your pack after *every* cursing attack.  Even if you
have both defences, there's a chance that your blessed unicorn horn is 
now a cursed unicorn horn.

On the other hand, a two-handed-weapon quest artifact is *unlikely* to be
taken from blessed to cursed in a single turn even if this does happen;
intelligent artifacts have 80% resistance to cursing.
